MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The ceramic capacitors fit the small circuits I have bought breadboards, PCB parts, and relay modules to build.",
    "Test leads with clips and hooks would help me check board connections, while heat shrink would help insulate wire joints on projects using battery holders. Both support tasks suggested by my past purchases."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Printer filament assumes I own and use a 3D printer; my electronics purchases do not establish that need, let alone a need for orange filament.",
    "The specific M6 screws need a matching mounting task, and my caster purchase does not establish one. Buffing compound and a thousand small exam gloves also lack a clear use in my current projects."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The suggestions stretch my interest in practical projects into an assumed need for unrelated workshop supplies.",
    "Buying a particular hardware item seems to have been taken as a reason to suggest other hardware without knowing whether its dimensions or purpose fit my task."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "I care about a direct connection to building, testing, or insulating small electrical circuits more than a broad connection to making things.",
    "Relevance does not always mean I would buy now: I would wait for a specific need before choosing Zener voltages or a precision measuring tool, and I would start with one capacitor assortment rather than both."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The suggestions understood my small electronics projects but stretched that interest too far into general workshop supplies and purchases without a current purpose."
}
